    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "35d1ebc595d3e46bef94bc5d3faf783c76ef7b8bd062bbee96d7cf4208fb9575",
      "text": "Today you’ll visit the Pemón indigenous community, enjoy a musical performance, shop for local handicrafts, and sample traditional cuisine — such as ant sauce, Moriche palm caterpillars, and cassava bread (casabe) made from yucca.\n\nMeals: Breakfast, lunch, dinner\n\nOptional excursions:\n\nVisit to the Kavac Canyon and a scenic flight over Angel Falls (half-day)\n\nHelicopter tour to Angel Falls (1 hour)\n\nBlue Lagoon (3 hours)\n\nBlue Lagoon & hike to Kuravaina Tepui (full day)\n\nSakaika Waterfall by bicycle (half-day)\n\nImportant note: Some excursions require good physical condition and involve trekking and long boat rides.\n\nDuring the dry season (February–May), when river levels are lower, we recommend the overnight expedition to Angel Falls (2 days / 1 night), with accommodation in hammocks.",
      "provenance": {
